    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d638">

                <pb facs="1183" n="1151" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v13p1/pg1151"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751G.00/3–2454: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Dillon</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Department of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-03-24T12:00:00+01:00">March 24,
                        1954—noon.</date><lb/>[Received 10:19 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3500. Repeated information Saigon 398. Last night at dinner with Laniel he said he was much more encouraged
                    regarding Indochina <pb facs="1184" n="1152" xml:id="pg1152"/> situation. The
                    action at Dien Bien Phu had, he said, greatly improved morale in France and the
                    spirit of defeatism, which had been rampant only a month ago, was now much more
                    subdued.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Dillon</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
